# DigiStream Cline repository rules

For all work, read root `AGENTS.md` first.

For any frontend/UI/UX/design-system work, mandatory read order:

1. `apps/web/AGENTS.md`
2. `docs/design/DIGISTREAM_UI_CONSTITUTION.md`
3. `docs/design/BEAUTIFUL_UI_ADAPTATION_STANDARD.md`
4. `docs/design/DIGISTREAM_AI_IMPLEMENTATION_GUARDRAILS.md`
5. `docs/design/DESIGN_TOKENS.md`
6. `docs/design/REFERENCE_INDEX.md`
7. relevant product/lifecycle/quality docs referenced by root `AGENTS.md`
8. existing implementation/tests

External UI reference: `https://beautiful-ui-five.vercel.app/`

## Mandatory visual rule

Preserve DigiStream's warm cream dotted application canvas. Build clean white/warm-white/neutral operational surfaces on top. Keep dusty pink as the primary brand accent. Use restrained lavender/sky/mint/amber/peach supporting tints only with intentional mapping. Keep live/success/warning/danger/info semantic colours fixed to real product meaning.

Adapt Beautiful UI patterns where they fit real responsibilities:

- Sidebar Nav -> creator workspace navigation
- Search -> authorized command/resource search
- Task Rows -> readiness/progress/recovery
- Filter/Records Tables -> Broadcasts, Recordings, admin/team/session records
- Loading State -> real async waits
- Approval Card -> consequential actions
- Chat -> Studio Lobby/live human communication
- Context Cards -> selected-resource context
- Insight Cards -> trustworthy analytics only
- Recommendation Card -> evidence-backed operational guidance only
- Tool Chips -> secondary diagnostics
- Selection Actions -> real supported bulk actions only

Do not copy Beautiful UI's AI Thinking/model picker/prompt/reasoning UI unless DigiStream gains an explicit real AI feature.

Do not remove the cream dotted identity to create generic SaaS UI. Do not make every component a giant cream/pink card with heavy shadow either.

Reuse current routes/components/APIs. Search `apps/web/src/design-system/` before creating a new primitive. Never invent metrics, listener counts, progress, permissions, lifecycle state, recordings, replay availability, media readiness or success.

Before changing product copy, search tests/docs for protected language. Preserve distinctions such as `Studio Lobby`, private contribution vs public delivery, scheduled vs live, and completed broadcast vs recording/replay ready.

All changed UI must preserve responsive/accessibility behavior and relevant tests. A redesign is not permission to weaken product, lifecycle or accessibility acceptance coverage.
